{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The protected observation `y` is a top-level data variable and is observed exactly once with a plain built-in sampling statement, after the parameter priors for `alpha` and `beta`. Context data variables `M`, `N`, `x0`, and `X` are used only for sizes and predictors.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> M; // Number of covariates
  int<lower=0> N; // Number of observations

  vector[M] x0;   // Covariate baselines
  matrix[N, M] X; // Covariate design matrix

  array[N] int y;       // Variates
}

transformed data {
  matrix[N, M] deltaX;
  for (n in 1:N) {
    deltaX[n,] = X[n] - x0';
  }
}

parameters {
  real alpha;      // Intercept
  vector[M] beta;  // Slopes
}

model {
  // Prior model
  alpha ~ normal(25, 5);
  beta ~ normal(0, 3);

  // Vectorized observation model
  y ~ poisson(alpha + deltaX * beta);
}

// Simulate a full observation from the current value of the parameters
generated quantities {
  vector[N] mu = alpha + deltaX * beta;
  array[N] int y_pred = poisson_rng(mu);
}
